From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Biggart <swbiggart@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:51:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/46] flashnext cuda: collectives on a blocking split of the
 nonblocking communicator

Every collective on a nonblocking communicator ran its launch on a thread of NCCL's and returned in progress, so
the engine polled it with a 50 us sleep, about 105 us a collective and 192 a decode pass. The parent stays nonblocking
and bounds start-up under the control link and a deadline as before; a blocking communicator split from it, sharing
its connections, carries every collective and returns once the kernel is enqueued. NCCL_RUNTIME_CONNECT=0, set when
unset, makes NCCL connect inside the parent's init and the split's job, which the parent's poll bounds, so no
collective waits on its peer for a connection. Abort ends the parent, which stops a split in flight, then the split.
